Package: RDataScienceCompendium
Title: Reproducible Resampling, Simulation and Model-Evaluation Methods
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Satvik", "Praveen", , "satvikpraveen707@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A research compendium of rigorously tested implementations of
    core statistical methods for applied data science: nonparametric bootstrap
    confidence intervals (percentile, basic, normal and bias-corrected and
    accelerated; Efron 1987 <doi:10.1080/01621459.1987.10478410>), Monte Carlo
    and exact permutation tests with valid p-values (Phipson and Smyth 2010
    <doi:10.2202/1544-6115.1585>), standardised effect sizes with exact
    noncentral-t confidence intervals, a reproducible framework for simulation
    studies that reports performance measures with Monte Carlo standard errors
    (Morris, White and Crowther 2019 <doi:10.1002/sim.8086>), and honest model
    evaluation via stratified, grouped and nested cross-validation together with
    discrimination and calibration metrics (DeLong, DeLong and Clarke-Pearson
    1988 <doi:10.2307/2531595>).
